# List dividers are `moh-divide`

Do not pick a divider color. Do not use Tailwind `divide-y`.

Tailwind `divide-y` without a `divide-*` color uses `currentColor`. In dark
mode that is near-white text, so every row gets a high-contrast white line.
Putting `moh-border` on the parent does **not** color those child borders.

## Use this

```vue
<ul class="moh-divide">
  <li class="moh-gutter-x py-3">…</li>
</ul>
```

`moh-divide` is defined in `assets/css/main.css` and always uses
`--moh-border-subtle`.

## Never

```vue
<!-- currentColor → white lines in dark mode -->
<ul class="divide-y">
<ul class="divide-y moh-border">

<!-- still a color decision; use moh-divide -->
<ul class="divide-y divide-gray-200 dark:divide-zinc-800">
```

Section chrome (tab bars, sticky headers, composers) may use
`border-b moh-border`. That is a single edge, not a list of rows.
